# Features & Services (always)

Resume: `@features$` / `$beta$`. Shipped in **s3.0.108**; access matrix + per-feature beta RBAC + sign-in redirect in **s3.0.110** (sections below marked s3.0.110 win over older text).

Master Admin → **Features & Services** decides which Search link buttons exist for whom. Only **ShoutOut** is live by default. Everything else is a **test feature** until a Master Admin turns it Live.

## Data model (Firestore)

| Collection | Doc | Key fields | Read | Write |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| `featureServices` | `{featureKey}` | `IsFeatureEnabled` 0\|1, `IsTestFeature` 0\|1, `revision`, `updatedByEmail`, `updatedAtMs`, `lastChangeReason` | signed in | Functions only |
| `betaTesters` | `{uid}` | `IsBetaTester` 0\|1, `status` active\|revoked, `role: "betaTester"`, **`features` {key: 0\|1}** (s3.0.110), `featuresUpdatedAtMs`, `featuresUpdatedByEmail`, `inviteId`, `invitedByEmail`, `acceptedAtMs`, `revokedByEmail`, `revokeReason` | self + Master Admin | Functions only |
| `betaInvites` | `sha256("floqr-beta-invite:"+token)` | `targetUid`, **`features`** (grant applied on accept), `status` pending\|accepted\|declined\|revoked, `expiresAtMs` (7 days), `createdByEmail` | Master Admin | Functions only |
| `featureServiceAccessThrottle` | `{uid}` | window start + count for `logFeatureAccessAttempt` (20 / 10 min) | nobody | Functions only |
| `featureServiceAuditLogs` | auto | see Audit | Master Admin | Functions only |
| `featureServiceAuditHead` | `current` | `hash`, `seq`, `eventId` | Master Admin | Functions only |

Feature keys (catalog in `functions/feature-services-core.js`, mirrored in `floqr-feature-services.js`; a test asserts parity): `shoutOut` {1,0}, `mingl`, `bartr`, `rydr`, `supRstar`, `floqAi` {0,1}. Missing doc → packaged default (fail closed for non-ShoutOut). Master Admin auto-seeds missing docs on first unlock (`seedFeatureServices`).

## Access matrix (s3.0.110 — by design, owner-confirmed)

The two switches sit side by side on each Features & Services row. `IsFeatureEnabled` is the master switch; `IsTestFeature` only means something when `IsFeatureEnabled = 1`. A feature can have passed testing and still sit parked with `IsFeatureEnabled = 0` — the Beta flag is **not** applied then.

| IsFeatureEnabled | IsTestFeature | state | Regular patron | Beta tester granted this feature | Master Admin |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| 0 | 0 or 1 | `off` | nothing | nothing | nothing (page + server denied); F&S row shows “Off” instead of the Open link |
| 1 | 1 | `test` | hidden / denied | **Search tile** (Beta pill) + page + server | **no Search tile**; opens it from the F&S **Master Admin link**; page + server allowed |
| 1 | 0 | `live` | yes | yes | yes |

```
state        = IsFeatureEnabled != 1 ? "off" : (IsTestFeature == 1 ? "test" : "live")
hasBetaGrant = !isMasterAdmin && betaTesters/{uid}.IsBetaTester==1 && status=="active" && features[key]==1
canAccess    = off → false · live → true · test → isMasterAdmin || hasBetaGrant      (pages + server)
searchVisible= off → false · live → true · test → hasBetaGrant                       (Search tiles; Master Admins excluded)
Search tile shown = searchVisible && legacy patronFeatureGates.patronMayUse
```

Server: `featureState` / `canAccessFeature` / `searchTileVisible` / `betaGrantsFrom` in `functions/feature-services-core.js`. Client mirror: `stateOf` / `canAccess` / `searchVisible` / `hasBetaGrant` / `betaGrantsFrom` in `floqr-feature-services.js`. `feature-services-core.test.js` runs the full matrix against **both** (server + vm-loaded client).

**RBAC — Master Admins and beta testers are disjoint roles.** A privileged account (`isPrivilegedProfile`: admin email list or `users.superAdmin` / master-admin role fields) can never be a beta tester: `createBetaInvite` refuses (unchained `beta.invite_denied`), `acceptBetaInvite` refuses, and `viewerFor` forces `isBetaTester=false` even if a stale `betaTesters` row exists. A beta tester gets **only the features ticked for them** (`features` map). ShoutOut is never a beta feature (`BETA_ELIGIBLE_KEYS`).

**Legacy testers (pre-s3.0.110)** have no `features` map → they see **no** test feature (fail closed). Master Admin must tick features and press **Save feature access** (`setBetaTesterFeatures`).

Enforcement points:

1. **Search tiles** — `index.html` ships non-ShoutOut tiles with `hidden`; `patron-app.js` `continueToMainCategories` → `FLOQRFeatureServices.load` + `applySearchUi` (runs after `applyPatronGateUi`) using `searchVisible`. Test tiles get `.feature-beta` pill (`cat.betaPill`). `?start=intent` now redirects to `floqai.html` (s3.1.20, guarded page — see `design-notes-floqai-page.mdc`); the in-index fallback to categories stays as a safety net.
2. **Satellite pages** — `<body data-floqr-feature="key">` + `floqr-feature-services.js`: hides body until checked. **Signed out → `FLOQRSessionShell.redirectToLogin()`** (general sign-in, see below); `data-floqr-feature-signed-out="allow"` was removed everywhere in s3.0.110. Signed in but denied → “This feature isn't available on your account yet.” + Back to Search, and `logFeatureAccessAttempt` records it. 8 s timeout = deny. Guarded: `commerce.html` (bartr), `pickup.html` + `rydr.html` (rydr), `suprstr-search.html` + `suprstar-preview.html` (supRstar), `mingl-chat.html` + `mingl-gist.html` (mingl).
3. **Server** — `assertFeatureAccess(auth, key)` in `createFloqrCheckoutSession` (`CHECKOUT_FEATURE_KEYS`) and `requestTeslaRobotaxiPickup`; denial detail carries `state` + `surface: "server"`. Client guards are UX; the server check is the control.

## Sign-in redirect on every page (s3.0.110)

A forwarded / bookmarked URL opened while signed out must land on the **general** FLOQR sign-in (Search Welcome card: Google, Microsoft, Facebook, Email, SMS, WhatsApp) — never a Google-only card.

- URL contract: `./?v=<APP_V>&profileRequired=sign-in&returnTo=<file?query#hash>` — same shape as `profile-access-guard.js` (hubs). `patron-app.js` `safeReturnTo` validates it (same-origin relative file only) and returns there after sign-in; Welcome status shows `app.signInToContinue`.
- `floqr-session-shell.js`: `loginHref()`, `redirectToLogin()`, and `requireSignIn()` which **auto-runs on every page that loads the shell** (even pages that never call `bind`). It never calls `initializeApp` — it polls ≤ 4 s for an existing Firebase app (many page apps call `initializeApp` unguarded), then waits ≤ 15 s for the persisted user.
- `bind()` no longer shows a Google button on standalone signed-out pages; it redirects instead.
- **Never redirect:** iframes / `embed=1` / `from=portal` (they keep the “open My Profile” link), and public pages: `index`, `display`, `display2`, `display-error`, `privacy`, `translation-policy`, `auth-debug`, or any page with `<body data-floqr-public>`.
- Hubs keep `profile-access-guard.js`; `club-profile` keeps its own redirect. s3.0.110 added the shell to `rydr.html`, `onboard-dc-venues.html`, `seed*.html`, `mobile-test-checklist.html`, `firestore-rebrand-*.html` (the `migrations/` copies are not served paths and were left alone).
- New satellite = load the shell after `firebase-config.js`; nothing else is needed for the redirect.

New feature checklist: add to both catalogs + `buttonIds`, add `data-feature-key` tile (hidden), guard its satellite page, add `assertFeatureAccess` to its paid/stateful callables, help + i18n.

## Callables (`functions/feature-services-functions.js`, us-central1)

All admin callables require an **SOS2FA** session (`assertSos2faSession`, scope `entityManagement`); failures log `*.denied` (unchained).

`setFeatureServiceFlags` (reason ≥ 8 chars, transaction: doc + chained audit) · `seedFeatureServices` · `createBetaInvite` (`featureKeys` required, ≥ 1 eligible key; privileged target refused; Inbox row `type: betaInvite` lists the features, link `./beta-invite.html?t=…`) · `acceptBetaInvite` / `declineBetaInvite` (patron, token must match `targetUid`; accept writes `features` + `role`, refuses Master Admins) · **`setBetaTesterFeatures`** (s3.0.110; SOS2FA, reason, active tester only, “Nothing changed” guard, chained `beta.features_changed` with before/after) · `revokeBetaTester` (reason; voids pending invites) · `revokeBetaInvite` · `logFeatureCodePromotion` (returns GitHub workflow URL) · `verifyFeatureServiceAuditChain`.

Patron-side logging callable **`logFeatureAccessAttempt({featureKey, page})`** (s3.0.110): signed-in only; transactional throttle 20 / 10 min per uid in `featureServiceAccessThrottle`; the **server re-evaluates** access and writes an unchained `feature.page_denied` row only when access really is denied (client cannot forge an “allowed” row or flood the chain).

## Beta testers

- Master Admin searches patrons (client scan of `users`, 500), ticks **Features this tester may use** (`#betaInviteFeatures`) → **Invite** → Inbox message + link copied to clipboard (share by any channel).
- Tester list shows per-feature checkboxes + **Save feature access** (reason prompt → `setBetaTesterFeatures`).
- `beta-invite.html` shows the granted features after Accept, or “Master Admins cannot be beta testers” (`beta.masterAdmin`).
- Token: 32 random bytes (base64url); only its SHA-256 is stored. Link is useless on another account (`wrong-account`), after 7 days, or once used. `beta-invite.html` strips `t` from the address bar after responding and sets `no-referrer`.
- Inbox button label: **Review beta invite** (`patron-portal-app.js` `inboxLinkLabel`).

## Test branch and promotion

GitHub Pages serves **one** branch (`main`). So runtime flags are the real gate (trunk-based dark launch): test code can live on `main` behind `IsTestFeature`.

- `test` branch = staging code line created from `main`. `sync-main-into-test.yml` merges every push to `main` into `test` (fails loudly on conflict).
- `functions-ci.yml` runs tests on pushes/PRs to `test`.
- `promote-test-to-main.yml` (workflow_dispatch, inputs reason + `PROMOTE`): i18n gate + Functions tests on `test` → `merge --no-ff` into `main` → fast-forward `test` → request Pages build → dispatch Functions CI. Functions **deploy** stays a separate `deploy=true` dispatch.
- Master Admin **Record promotion & open workflow** writes `code.promotion_requested` (chained) and opens the workflow page. No GitHub PAT is stored in Functions.
- Order: promote code → set `IsFeatureEnabled` = 1 + `IsTestFeature` = 1 (beta testers try it on Search) → verify → set `IsTestFeature` = 0 (live for everyone). Setting `IsFeatureEnabled` = 0 parks it for everyone (Master Admins included) without losing the Test flag.

## Audit (ISO/IEC 27001:2022 + NIST SP 800-53 Rev. 5)

Record fields (`buildAuditRecord`): `eventType`, `outcome` success|failure|denied, `actorUid`, `actorEmail`, `actorRole`, `targetType`, `targetId`, `before`, `after`, `reason`, `detail`, `sos2faSessionHash` (sha256/16), `sourceIpTruncated` (/24 or /48), `sourceIpHash`, `userAgent`, `source`, `createdAtMs`, `createdAtIso` (UTC), server `createdAt`, `controlSets`, `retentionYears` 7, `expireAtMs`.

| Control | How |
|---|---|
| A.8.15 / AU-2, AU-12 | Every flag, seed, invite, accept/decline, revoke, promotion, verify, and denial is logged by the server |
| AU-3 | what / when / where / source / outcome / identity + before/after |
| AU-8 / A.8.17 | Server clock, ISO-8601 UTC + serverTimestamp |
| AU-9 / A.8.15 | Rules: no client writes; Master Admin read only; SHA-256 hash chain (`prevHash`, `seq`, head doc in same transaction) |
| AU-10 | Actor uid/email + SOS2FA session hash bound into the chained hash |
| AU-11 | 7-year retention (`expireAtMs`) — do **not** enable a Firestore TTL shorter than this |
| CM-3 / A.8.32 | Reason required, revision counter, before/after, promotion log |
| AC-6(9) | Denied privileged attempts logged |
| A.8.16 | **Verify integrity** button; chain verdict itself is logged |

Denials are unchained on purpose (no contention on the head doc from abusive traffic).

