## Proposal — fork into an Admin app and a Patron app (owner-requested s3.0.110, not built yet)

Goal: admins and patrons stop sharing one login path and one origin. Patrons keep today’s Welcome card; admins get a separate, hardened console. Beta testers stay **patrons** with extra RBAC grants — they never touch the admin app.

### Target shape

| | Patron app (current) | Admin app (new) |
|---|---|---|
| Origin | `https://www.floqr.com` (cutover) | `https://admin.floqr.com` (separate Firebase Hosting **site** in the same project; not GitHub Pages) |
| Pages | Search, My Profile, satellites, Display | `master-admin.html`, Club Admin console (`admin.html`), promoter admin, diagnostics, seed/onboarding tools |
| Sign-in | Google / Microsoft / Facebook / Email / SMS (US+CA) / WhatsApp | **Workforce only:** Google Workspace or Microsoft Entra SSO (OIDC/SAML) **plus** a passkey / security key (WebAuthn) — no SMS, no WhatsApp, no Facebook |
| Auth tenant | Identity Platform tenant `patrons` (or default) | Identity Platform tenant `admins` (multi-tenancy) — a patron account literally cannot sign in here |
| Session | Firebase persistence on www | Short session (e.g. 8 h idle 30 min) + **SOS2FA step-up** kept for dangerous actions |
| App Check | reCAPTCHA Enterprise key for www | Separate App Check key for admin origin; Functions enforce `enforceAppCheck` for admin callables |
| Network | public | Optional IP allowlist / Cloud Armor (Hosting behind a load balancer) for the admin site |

### Authorization model (replaces email lists)

- **Custom claims**, set only by Functions: `role: "masterAdmin" | "venueAdmin" | "serviceMember"`, `venueIds: [...]`, `tenant: "admins"`. Beta testers get `betaFeatures: ["bartr", ...]` on the **patron** tenant only.
- Admin callables check `request.auth.token.firebase.tenant === "admins"` **and** the role claim. Patron callables reject the admin tenant for patron-only flows (no admin placing patron orders as a shortcut).
- Firestore rules: `request.auth.token.role == "masterAdmin"` replaces `isMasterAdminEmail()` and deletes the email lists (the `bands.don` / `bans.don` mismatch itself was already fixed in s3.1.26: single spelling `bans.don@gmail.com`).
- Disjoint roles stay enforced: granting `betaFeatures` refuses any uid that holds an admin claim; creating an admin removes beta grants.

### Migration in phases (each phase shippable on its own)

1. **Claims first (no UX change):** a `syncRoleClaims` callable/trigger writes claims from today’s sources (admin lists, `users.superAdmin`, `betaTesters.features`, club admin designations). Rules + callables accept claim **or** legacy check. Force token refresh after changes.
2. **Rules on claims only:** remove email lists from `firestore.rules`, `sos2fa`, `PRIVILEGED_EMAILS`; restrict `users` + `inboxNotifications` reads (open findings 1–2).
3. **Admin Hosting site:** `firebase.json` gets a second `hosting` target (`admin`) serving only admin pages; add `admin.floqr.com` to Auth authorized domains, OAuth clients, App Check. Keep the old paths on Pages redirecting to the admin origin.
4. **Admin tenant + SSO + passkeys:** create the `admins` tenant, move admin accounts, admin login page offers SSO + passkey only. SOS2FA remains as step-up.
5. **Split bundles:** patron bundle drops admin JS entirely (no `master-admin-app.js` on www); admin bundle drops patron satellites. Shared code (`shared-data.js`, i18n, help) published as versioned modules both sides load.
6. **Retire the shared path:** admin pages removed from the patron origin; `profile-access-guard.js` on www no longer knows about admin roles.

Risks / notes: two authorized domains to maintain; Club Admins who are also patrons need **two accounts** (one per tenant) — document it in Club Admin help; Xibo Display URLs are unaffected (they stay on the patron/display origin, no `?v=`); deep links in admin emails must point at `admin.floqr.com`.

